n":null,"kind":"theorem","line":355,"note":"","open_assumptions":[],"premises":[],"reached":false,"relation":"unassessed","review_evidence":"not_reviewed","reviewed_by":null,"reviewed_relation":"unassessed","reviewed_route":"unassessed","route":"unassessed","wrapper_comparison_evidence":"not_run"},{"build_evidence":"current","built":true,"compared":false,"comparison_credit":"none","comparison_evidence":"not_run","configured_checks":[],"declaration":"QuarticQuery.Upper.prepOf","declaration_lines":[47,63],"file":"lean/QuarticQuery/Upper/Amplify.lean","hypotheses":[],"inspection":null,"kind":"def","line":49,"note":"A unitary, a basis start and a label set as a Preparation.","open_assumptions":[],"premises":[],"reached":true,"relation":"unassessed","review_evidence":"legacy_unbound","reviewed_by":"ai:truth-auditor","reviewed_relation":"partial","reviewed_route":"none","route":"unassessed","wrapper_comparison_evidence":"not_run"},{"build_evidence":"current","built":true,"compared":false,"comparison_credit":"none","comparison_evidence":"not_run","configured_checks":[],"declaration":"QuarticQuery.Upper.lawOf_iterate_some","declaration_lines":[201,229],"file":"lean/QuarticQuery/Upper/Amplify.lean","hypotheses":[],"inspection":null,"kind":"theorem","line":203,"note":"After l iterations a successful label keeps the sampler's law, scaled by the success mass. Law form of 'independently of l'.","open_assumptions":[],"premises":[],"reached":true,"relation":"unassessed","review_evidence":"legacy_unbound","reviewed_by":"ai:truth-auditor","reviewed_relation":"partial","reviewed_route":"same","route":"unassessed","wrapper_comparison_evidence":"not_run"},{"build_evidence":"current","built":true,"compared":false,"comparison_credit":"none","comparison_evidence":"not_run","configured_checks":[],"declaration":"QuarticQuery.Upper.Samples.attempts","declaration_lines":[245,343],"file":"lean/QuarticQuery/Upper/Amplify.lean","hypotheses":["M<>0"],"inspection":null,"kind":"theorem","line":247,"note":"Trials on a sampler as a program on the bit oracle, each a full measurement followed by a reset to the start state, in place of fresh registers. Law on success exact; failure probability the t-th power of one trial's.","open_assumptions":["M<>0"],"premises":[],"reached":true,"relation":"unassessed","review_evidence":"legacy_unbound","reviewed_by":"ai:truth-auditor","reviewed_relation":"partial","reviewed_route":"same","route":"unassessed","wrapper_comparison_evidence":"not_run"},{"build_evidence":"current","built":true,"compared":false,"comparison_credit":"none","comparison_evidence":"not_run","configured_checks":[],"declaration":"QuarticQuery.Upper.Samples.amplify","declaration_lines":[345,359],"file":"lean/QuarticQuery/Upper/Amplify.lean","hypotheses":["0<gamma","0<eta"],"inspection":null,"kind":"theorem","line":346,"note":"Lemma 3.1 on the bit oracle, for samplers: cap, eta failure when p>=gamma, certain failure at p=0, and the exact law on success labels. It states a label law, not the state |g>, and it is for circuits, not black-box. This, not bounded_amplification, is what Q_Fkm_le consumes.","open_assumptions":["0<gamma","0<eta"],"premises":[],"reached":true,"relation":"unassessed","review_evidence":"legacy_unbound","reviewed_by":"ai:truth-auditor","reviewed_relation":"partial","reviewed_route":"same","route":"unassessed","wrapper_comparison_evidence":"not_run"},{"build_evidence":"current","built":true,"compared":false,"comparison_credit":"none","comparison_evidence":"not_run","configured_checks":[],"declaration":"QuarticQuery.Upper.trialCount_le","declaration_lines":[20,34],"file":"lean/QuarticQuery/Upper/Bound.lean","hypotheses":[],"inspection":null,"kind":"theorem","line":21,"note":"Crude polynomial bound on the trial count, for budget_le.","open_assumptions":[],"premises":[],"reached":true,"relation":"unassessed","review_evidence":"legacy_unbound","reviewed_by":"ai:truth-auditor","reviewed_relation":"partial","reviewed_route":"none","route":"unassessed","wrapper_comparison_evidence":"not_run"},{"build_evidence":"current","built":true,"compared":false,"comparison_credit":"none","comparison_evidence":"not_run","configured_checks":[],"declaration":"QuarticQuery.Upper.iterationBound_inv_le","declaration_lines":[36,45],"file":"lean/QuarticQuery/Upper/Bound.lean","hypotheses":[],"inspection":null,"kind":"theorem","line":37,"note":"Bound on the iteration count, for budget_le.","open_assumptions":[],"premises":[],"reached":true,"relation":"unassessed","review_evidence":"legacy_unbound","reviewed_by":"ai:truth-auditor","reviewed_relation":"partial","reviewed_route":"none","route":"unassessed","wrapper_comparison_evidence":"not_run"}],"ledger_history":{"added_in_review":false,"adjudication_findings":[{"claim":"Preserve worst-branch cap and normalised successful state; randomised iteration count preserves the conditional density matrix.","id":"R2-LR4","paper_locus":"Lemma 3.1, pp.7-8","reason":"Eq. 8 scales the good component uniformly. See also M-1, which adds the missing quantifier.","verdict":"accepted"},{"claim":"Troy Lee's library has amplified_cond_law and a Grover state theorem.","id":"R3-LA-11","paper_locus":"Lemma 3.1","reason":"No local clone. The mathematical point stands: a conditional output law is enough for sampling and weaker than Lemma 3.1 as written.","verdict":"unverified"},{"claim":"Section 5: three amplification obligations; fresh workspaces for the product.","id":"R3-RF-05","paper_locus":"Lemma 3.1, Eq. 15","reason":"Mathematics accepted; library claims as R3-LA-11. M-1 adds a fourth.","verdict":"accepted"},{"claim":"Lemma 3.1 hides a quantifier: the procedure must be black-box in A, with call counts depending only on gamma, eta.","id":"M-1","paper_locus":"Lemma 3.1 lines 310-320; line 354 'Fix an input' and line 361 'pointwise'","reason":"Read literally, 'there is a procedure' for a given A allows dependence on p or theta, which depend on the oracle input and would break the query model. The proof is uniform (M, trial count). Prop 3.2 has the same literal issue; r3 flagged the order there, no return flagged it for Lemma 3.1. Needed: exists procedure, for all A.","verdict":"accepted"}],"earlier_ledger_wording":"Let A be a state preparation with a success bit, success probability p and, if p>0, normalized successful state |g>. For 0<gamma<=1/2 and 0<eta<1/2 there is a procedure using O(gamma^{-1/2} log(1/eta)) calls to A and A^{-1}, for every p and on every branch, that reports failure or produces a successful outcome. Conditional on success the output is |g> up to global phase. If p>=gamma, failure probability <=eta. If p=0 it always reports failure.","wording_changed":true},"original_statement_sha256":"b0707e8e25eb167389619d8a2d0fa8e0b836170755451369f00a2a91b141bdd4","passages":["CAT-lem-3.1"],"review_scope":{"compared_text":"maintained_ledger_statement","leading_matches":[{"declaration":"QuarticQuery.Amplification.bounded_amplification","file":"lean/QuarticQuery/Amplification/Bounded.lean"}],"relation_origin":"authored_review","semantic_examples":"none_indexed","type_and_axioms_origin":"compiled_lean_environment"},"section":"3.1","semantic_probes":[],"source_line":310,"statement":"For 0<gamma<=1/2 and 0<eta<1/2 there is a single procedure, black-box in A and A^{-1} and with call counts depending only on gamma and eta, using O(gamma^{-1/2} log(1/eta)) calls for every p and on every branch, such that for every state preparation A with a success bit, success probability p and, if p>0, normalized successful state |g>: it reports failure or produces a successful outcome; conditional on success the output is |g> up to global phase; if p>=gamma, failure probability <=eta; if p=0 it always reports failure.","statement_sha256":"b76e3c7f8a37dd0cdf934b72d91d1ad52678f354374884a3666bc12236871ec8"}
